{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "07WW", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-change-of-field}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:da0c0663077e629c7be2be1a8a3e71f6a59ecbad7584f40fae95b6dc7e581054", "source_text": "Change of field", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76a11a670705f07341d3f6fc833771d16f9839e793c931780d0f4cbdd5b1232c", "unit_id": "tag:07WW:title"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07WW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, k}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}_{l/k}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{formal-defos-section-change-of-field}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{formal-defos-situation-change-of-fields}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3e62e9c1399838698801aa76ea3ca4c6bd4013fc7917c16dec74d9f1355ba093", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fbf4cf15a515ec97bbe6142e712f8b998e78f8d3bea87d9eb14183960534116a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the analogue of\nFormal Deformation Theory, Section <REF_0001>.\nAs pointed out there, to discuss what happens under change of field\nwe need to write <MATH_0001> instead of <MATH_0002>.\nIn the following lemma we use the notation <MATH_0003>\nintroduced in Formal Deformation Theory, Situation\n<REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f13ddef2c19f547981128ed8b90ceb85d8f3ffe86b770220cbc4b1ecce6d6a18", "unit_id": "tag:07WW:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07WW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$l/k$", "MATH_0007": "$x_0$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$x_{l, 0}$", "MATH_0011": "$x_0$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Spec(l)$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n(\\mathcal{F}_{\\mathcal{X}, k , x_0})_{l/k}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}_{\\mathcal{X}, l, x_{l, 0}}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, l}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{X}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-change-of-field}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:10cac00b701a7ee18dd1fd615307eb0f78e08ea59778f1fe661a9dbcfea47f6e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:27f7bdba659940ff7be9d3ec4671e0b84ccdb40ff7b133aac4413d21f8f2c2e3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004> be a\nfield of finite type over <MATH_0005> and let <MATH_0006> be a finite extension.\nLet <MATH_0007> be an object of <MATH_0008> lying over <MATH_0009>.\nDenote <MATH_0010> the restriction of <MATH_0011> to <MATH_0012>.\nThen there is a canonical functor\n<MATH_0013>\nof categories cofibred in groupoids over <MATH_0014>.\nIf <MATH_0015> satisfies (RS), then this functor is an equivalence.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:24cbcf4a8690915c46dedd34bf176c0522d108398ef81f41ad13ad90e6d79a0e", "unit_id": "tag:07WX:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "categories.tex", "kind": "section", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 242287, "start": 242277}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 242359, "start": 242149}, "container_hash": "sha256:5e5c65214fc77b4f09f86b1bce6c25714697de4be2e8e78c1a2637d6f027befe"}, {"command_byte_span": {"end": 242783, "start": 242773}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 242847, "start": 242659}, "container_hash": "sha256:c56690e42ba08b833426b2187a56e6527ac6172fb9b61653b212c3400b48a67f"}, {"command_byte_span": {"end": 243361, "start": 243351}, "command_hash": "sha256:fd3d664c90c8644f5970c6b1608b04e5cf1fc7984e8c9b92c1131eba0cfd124a", "container_byte_span": {"end": 243453, "start": 243199}, "container_hash": "sha256:22bd2849d377c2382ec7d8e17d3577c7f8754022db5b490d58106c1c7300a2de"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "categories-section-inertia", "owner_tag": "04Z2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:4108cf525225a3a755d96ea80bf1b4fb421350b56ee9543c0b8ab97e2eaa3f9f", "source_label": "categories-section-inertia", "usage": "quad-connector", "usage_source": {"after": "\\quad", "before": "\\quad", "environments": []}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "connective-and", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 96, "start": 93}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": "and"}], "source": "$$\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\nl & B \\ar[l] \\\\\nk \\ar[u] & B \\times_l k \\ar[l] \\ar[u]\n}\n}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(l) \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\Spec(B) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(k) \\ar[r] & \\Spec(B \\times_l k)\n}\n}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 1060, "start": 848}, "source_hash": "sha256:4bd35fca6d3cf90c4e50ee362582e6a3aca78c5a3effc8e66ef19ae7d5cf4801"}], "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07WW", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\nl & B \\ar[l] \\\\\nk \\ar[u] & B \\times_l k \\ar[l] \\ar[u]\n}\n}\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(l) \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\Spec(B) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(k) \\ar[r] & \\Spec(B \\times_l k)\n}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\Spec(l) \\to \\Spec(B) \\to S\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n(\\mathcal{F}_{\\mathcal{X}, k , x_0})_{l/k}(B) =\n\\mathcal{F}_{\\mathcal{X}, k, x_0}(B \\times_l k)\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$x_0 \\to x$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(k) \\to \\Spec(B \\times_l k)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$x_0 \\to x$", "MATH_0008": "$x_{l, 0} \\to x_B$", "MATH_0009": "$x_B$", "MATH_0010": "$x$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Spec(B)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(B \\times_l k)$", "MATH_0013": "$B \\times_l k \\subset B$", "MATH_0014": "$B$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0016": "$S$", "MATH_0017": "$$\n\\mathcal{X}_{\\Spec(B \\times_l k)}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{X}_{\\Spec(k)}\n\\times_{\\mathcal{X}_{\\Spec(l)}}\n\\mathcal{X}_{\\Spec(B)}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-factor}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{formal-defos-situation-change-of-fields}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-pushout-along-thickening}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{definition-RS}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{categories-lemma-equivalence-fibred-categories}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:68b1f20f15f9fa22544dca5688db1c4fca72289f54b56b1c5d5b0d4b7284697a", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:987334471cce9a55167fe3f813b84db44d6e389773b9233b910d4d8fb35fcfa9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1534963a6199912d50266e352f09e0509d673352a5187989cd2933094536d158", "source_text": "Consider a factorization\n<MATH_0001>\nas in (<REF_0001>). By definition we have\n<MATH_0002>\nsee Formal Deformation Theory, Situation\n<REF_0002>. Thus an object of this\nis a morphism <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004> lying over the morphism\n<MATH_0005>. Choosing pullback functor for <MATH_0006>\nwe can associate to <MATH_0007> the morphism <MATH_0008>\nwhere <MATH_0009> is the restriction of <MATH_0010> to <MATH_0011> (via the morphism\n<MATH_0012> coming from <MATH_0013>).\nThis construction is functorial in <MATH_0014> and compatible with morphisms.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nNext, assume <MATH_0015> satisfies (RS). Consider the diagrams\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nThe diagram on the left is a fibre product of rings. The diagram on the\nright is a pushout in the category of schemes, see\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThese schemes are all of finite type over <MATH_0016> (see remarks following\nDefinition <REF_0004>). Hence (RS) kicks in to give an equivalence\nof fibre categories\n<MATH_0017>\nThis implies that the functor defined above gives an equivalence of\nfibre categories. Hence the functor is an equivalence on categories\ncofibred in groupoids by (the dual of)\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:197296010bba961b4e8957a837eed412111e0fd7e2e1bbe31135fd71a5fec4c1", "unit_id": "tag:07WX:proof"}
